WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.119
<v Leo>Ninety seconds for a whole program?

00:00:03.139 --> 00:00:05.922
<v Leo>I've had meetings take longer to find the dial-in.

00:00:05.942 --> 00:00:07.092
<v Ava>Then let's beat them.

00:00:07.112 --> 00:00:08.766
<v Ava>Chip's got the stopwatch.

00:00:09.416 --> 00:00:11.516
<v Ava>Over twelve months, we document,

00:00:11.536 --> 00:00:16.062
<v Ava>approve and launch every HR policy, process and legal obligation.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.975
<v Leo>Across 13 jurisdictions?

00:00:17.995 --> 00:00:20.079
<v Leo>That's 438 items.

00:00:20.099 --> 00:00:23.384
<v Leo>And we tracked them in a spreadsheet called final_v7?

00:00:23.404 --> 00:00:25.025
<v Ava>Which is exactly the problem.

00:00:25.045 --> 00:00:29.100
<v Ava>For a public company, every gap is audit or legal exposure.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.495
<v Ava>Mobilize starts October 12:

00:00:31.515 --> 00:00:35.461
<v Ava>four weeks to set up the team, tools and approval chains.

00:00:35.481 --> 00:00:36.566
<v Leo>Then the waves.

00:00:36.586 --> 00:00:38.724
<v Leo>Let me guess, scariest stuff first?

00:00:38.744 --> 00:00:39.305
<v Ava>Yep.

00:00:39.325 --> 00:00:41.862
<v Ava>Wave 1 tackles the riskiest must-haves,

00:00:41.882 --> 00:00:46.560
<v Ava>Waves 2 and 3 finish every required item, and Wave 4 makes it stick.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.333
<v Leo>Done by October 8, 2027.

00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:51.215
<v Leo>Blocking my calendar now.

00:00:51.865 --> 00:00:53.172
<v Leo>Who's doing all this?

00:00:53.192 --> 00:00:54.591
<v Leo>Please don't say me.

00:00:54.611 --> 00:00:57.023
<v Ava>Six workstreams, each with a named lead.

00:00:57.043 --> 00:01:00.876
<v Ava>Regional and country HR leads handle the local details.

00:01:00.896 --> 00:01:04.535
<v Leo>Good, because Germany doesn't exactly run like Texas.

00:01:05.185 --> 00:01:08.563
<v Ava>Every item moves through five stages: discover what exists,

00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:11.049
<v Ava>then draft it in the standard template.

00:01:11.069 --> 00:01:14.911
<v Leo>Then review and approve, where my emails usually go to die.

00:01:14.931 --> 00:01:15.649
<v Ava>Not here.

00:01:15.669 --> 00:01:17.265
<v Ava>Approvals run in the Atlas.

00:01:17.285 --> 00:01:20.842
<v Ava>Go live means published, communicated and evidence filed.

00:01:21.492 --> 00:01:22.366
<v Leo>Last thing.

00:01:22.386 --> 00:01:23.985
<v Leo>Where do I find my stuff?

00:01:24.005 --> 00:01:25.837
<v Ava>Project HQ for the big picture,

00:01:25.857 --> 00:01:30.089
<v Ava>the Master checklist for your items, and Approvals for sign-offs.

00:01:30.739 --> 00:01:36.474
<v Ava>That's Atlas: 438 items, five stages, four waves, one place to track them.

00:01:36.494 --> 00:01:38.307
<v Leo>Ninety seconds, give or take.

00:01:38.327 --> 00:01:41.459
<v Leo>Next time, we find and update your items.
